# The exact version of every tool a gate installs to run (`uvx`,
# `uv tool run`, `uv run --with`), in one place.
#
# Given no version, `uvx` resolves the newest release on the day it runs, so
# two runs of the same gate can run two different scanners, and a range such
# as `mkdocs>=1.6,<2` builds a fresh environment whenever a release lands
# inside it. One exact version per tool keeps every run on one cached tool
# environment and makes a new release a reviewed change to this file.
#
# Read by, and never copied into:
#
#   * `kew/scripts/verify.sh` and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — the semgrep gate
#     (SEMGREP_VERSION, SETUPTOOLS_VERSION) and the license gate
#     (PIP_LICENSES_VERSION).
#   * `scripts/build-check-image.sh` — the semgrep kew's check image installs
#     (SEMGREP_VERSION, SETUPTOOLS_VERSION), passed to
#     `scripts/check-image.Dockerfile` as build arguments with no default.
#   * `scripts/check-docs.sh` and `www/deploy.sh` — the docs build
#     (MKDOCS_VERSION, MKDOCS_MATERIAL_VERSION).
#   * `.github/workflows/release.yml` — the release checks (TWINE_VERSION,
#     CYCLONEDX_BOM_VERSION).
#
# The semgrep and license commands a contributor copies out of AGENTS.md and
# CONTRIBUTING.md name their versions literally. tests/test_verify_parity.py
# holds every such call in a gate, and those copyable commands, equal to this
# file, and refuses any line outside it that sets a pinned name.
#
# This file is SOURCED by bash, read with awk where a script may source
# nothing (verify.sh), and read line-wise by tests, so it holds nothing but
# comments and plain assignments — no expansion, no command, no conditional,
# no export, no quotes.
SEMGREP_VERSION=1.182.1
SETUPTOOLS_VERSION=84.2.1
MKDOCS_VERSION=1.6.1
MKDOCS_MATERIAL_VERSION=9.7.7
TWINE_VERSION=7.0.0
CYCLONEDX_BOM_VERSION=7.5.0
PIP_LICENSES_VERSION=5.5.5
